#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:59
msgid "You know from [session 1](./01-intro-syntax-types.md#str-text) and 3: a string is a **sequence** of characters; `len(s)`, `s[0]`, `s[-1]`, `s[2:5]` work like on a list; `s[2:5]` is `SUBSTR(s, 3, 3)` in SAS. And a string **cannot change** (it is immutable): every method returns a **new** string."
