msgid "Spaces inside: `COMPBL`"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:165
msgid "`strip` does not touch the spaces **inside** a text. `split()` without an argument cuts the text into words at every group of spaces, and `\" \".join(...)` puts the words back with one space between them:"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:176
msgid "`\" \".join(s.split())` is the usual Python way to say \"remove all extra spaces\". Section 4 explains `split` and `join`."
