#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:714
msgid "For a simple test, use the string methods - they are clearer. For a shape, use a regex. In SAS the same patterns work with `PRXMATCH`; in SQL, `LIKE` does a small part of it and `REGEXP_LIKE` the rest."
msgstr ""

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:718
msgid "`re.search` and the match object"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:720
msgid "The module `re` comes with Python. `re.search(pattern, text)` looks for the first place where the pattern fits. It returns a **match object** - or `None` if the pattern fits nowhere:"
msgstr ""

