#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:1355
msgid "`\"1,234\"` - is it one thousand two hundred thirty-four (English), or one point two three four (Bulgarian)? The rule above says 1234, because three digits after the separator are thousands. In your own data, **ask** which format a source uses, and write it down - do not guess per value."
