#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:1394
msgid "`parse_amount(\"12,5\")` gives `12.5`: one digit after the comma, so the comma is the decimal separator. `parse_amount(\"1,234\")` gives `1234.0`: three digits after the comma, so the comma separates the thousands. For a source in the English format the first answer is wrong: there `12,5` cannot be a number at all, and a rule that accepts it hides a typing error."
