#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/07-text-and-regex.md:1429
msgid "`%b` and `%B` follow the **locale**. By default Python uses English month names, but if a program (or a library) switches the locale with `locale.setlocale`, `%b` expects the month names of that language, and `strptime(\"8 Jun 2014\", \"%d %b %Y\")` can fail. For data, prefer numeric formats. If a source has English month names, a small dictionary `{\"Jan\": 1, ...}` ([session 6](./06-dictionaries.md)) is the safe way."
